 "notes_text": "Emotional twin of the original's rocking opening, rebuilt on the appoggiatura sigh. Each hook downbeat is a dissonance on the soft, dark 'u' (Ab5 over the tonic, Eb5 over V6/5) that resolves by a semitone onto the bright 'a a' (G5 G5, then D5), so the followers' 'u a a' becomes sigh-and-answer. The harmony rocks one chord per bar between i and V6/5 over a C-B semitone bass: the whole texture sinks a semitone and comes back, a pendulum like the original's but not its C-D bass or its u-a-a cell. Bars 4-6 speed up with three new triplet shapes (a turn on beat 1, a lower-neighbour turn on beat 2, a rising diminished arpeggio F-Ab-B with the augmented second Ab-B) that carry the line by step to the one cry: C6 over V at 7.9 s (57 %), falling a semitone to B5 as a 4-3 suspension. The cadence is Phrygian: Neapolitan Db major, arpeggio Ab-F-Db, then the Db->C sigh; the tonic C5 arrives a triplet early (11.32 s) and is held while the waltz goes on, with V7 under it in the last bar so the auto-loop resolves into the pickup. Range C5-C6, wider than the brief's minor 7th because of the octave cry; 89 % of the notes sit inside Db5-Ab5."
